---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = '2026-07-27';
---

<Base title="Privacy — Entanglo" description="Entanglo runs entirely on your local network. No cloud, no telemetry, no account.">
  <section class="container-tight pt-20 pb-12">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent mb-3">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="display text-5xl md:text-6xl gradient-text leading-tight">
      Your Macs talk to each other. Nobody else.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-ink-700 text-lg">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container-tight py-10 space-y-10">
    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">What stays on your LAN</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        Every byte Entanglo moves — mouse events, clipboard text, files, screenshots, print jobs —
        travels directly between your own Macs over your home Wi-Fi or Ethernet. There is no
        Entanglo server in the middle. We never see your data, because there is no "we" in the path.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        The <strong>app</strong> collects nothing. No analytics, no crash reporter that phones home,
        no account system, no email signup. You don't tell us anything because we don't ask.
      </p>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        The <strong>website</strong> uses Cloudflare Web Analytics — see the "Updates" section
        below for what that means (aggregated, no cookies, no per-visitor profile).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">Permissions Entanglo asks for</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-800">
        <li><strong class="text-ink-950">Accessibility</strong> — required to inject mouse and keyboard events on the target Mac (CGEvent).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink-950">Local Network</strong> — required for Bonjour peer discovery and the TCP link.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink-950">Screen Recording</strong> — only if you use the "screenshot peer" Quick Action.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink-950">Apple Events</strong> — only when you explicitly use AppleScript-driven features.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">Pairing & trust</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        Trusted peers are stored in your macOS Keychain. Revoke a peer any time from the Pairing tab.
        Nothing about your trusted devices leaves your machine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">Updates</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        New versions are pushed peer-to-peer over your LAN, or downloaded from this website on demand.
        The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare may log your IP and User-Agent for
        the page request, per their standard service logs. The app itself does not contact this website.
      </p>

      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        This website uses <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> to count page views. It runs
        entirely on Cloudflare's edge, uses no cookies, does not fingerprint the browser, and stores
        only aggregated counts (page, referrer, country) — never a per-visitor profile.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">Ads on this website</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        This website may show ads (Google AdSense) to help cover hosting costs. Ads run only on the
        website, never inside the app. AdSense uses cookies — see Google's privacy notice for details.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink-950 mb-3">Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-800 leading-relaxed">
        Email <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="mailto:support@entanglo.app">support@entanglo.app</a> any time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
